<title>USA: No risk of systemic banking crisis -- Brazil's Malan.</title>
<headline>No risk of systemic banking crisis -- Brazil's Malan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian Finance Minister Pedro Malan Sunday dismissed concerns of an industry-wide banking crisis in his country.</p>
<p>&quot;Brazil is not confronted with any risk of systemic crisis,&quot; Malan told the International Monetary Fund's policy-making Interim Committee.</p>
<p>Banco Do Brasil has been strongly capitalized, he said, and Banco Meridional will be privatised in due course.</p>
<p>&quot;In the case of state banks, new legislation has been enacted with the objective of definitely overcoming the problems Brazil traditionally faced in this area,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
